AB  - Hyperspectral object tracking aims to capture object positions frame by frame using spectral information in scenarios where visual features are missing or disrupted. The existing prompt-based trackers perform well. However, these models lack sufficient time for information mining for video sequences and neglect fully using spectral information in the prompt generation stage. To address this issue, this paper proposes a Spectral-temporal Token-guided Tracker (STTrack) based on a Prompt Mamba Module (PMM). Specifically, a spectral token is proposed to capture spectral regions of interest in a time series, to guide tracker learning. In addition, a PMM is proposed to incorporate spectral information into the tracker. The module compresses the spatial and spectral representation with a state space model. In addition, to fully utilize the prior knowledge in the RGB domain, we fine-tuned STTrack and PMM on advanced RGB trackers. This not only improves the performance of our method but also enables us to process hyperspectral videos of any number of bands without consuming excessive training resources. Extensive comparison experiments on the HOTC-2024 dataset prove the effectiveness of our proposed methods.
