AB  - Satellite remote sensing technology has the ability to periodically obtain surface information, which can quickly extract dynamic changes in the surface. It is widely used in fields such as land and resources investigation, urban building extraction, and disaster monitoring. The research on identifying and predicting surface deformation in open-pit mines is of great significance for improving the precision of disaster warning and formulating safety prevention measures. Based on this, this article designs an intelligent recognition and prediction model that combines remote sensing technology and deep learning (DL) for mining surface changes. Firstly, a remote sensing change detection method based on time difference prompt SAM (Segment Anything Model) is adopted, utilizing the powerful visual recognition ability of SAM model to improve the change detection of remote sensing images. Then, the Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) algorithm and Long Short Term Memory (LSTM) model are introduced into the prediction of surface deformation in mining areas, and a PSO-LSTM prediction model is constructed to achieve accurate prediction of surface changes in mines. Simulation experiments show that this model can improve the recognition ability of network models for image difference information, and perform better in terms of the integrity and edge details of ground objects in the detection results, with higher prediction precision.
