AB  - To address the cross-domain detection challenges in heterogeneous Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) imagery, this paper proposes a teacher-student learning Transformer domain adaptation method starting from data. We argue that mining domain invariance and domain specificity directly from the data is a more effective strategy. Thus, the proposed method explicitly instructs the detector to achieve a global representation and enhances the inter-class distinguishability of instance-level features across the entire dataset spanning two domains by utilizing contrast learning. Through six object detection experiments on heterogeneous SAR and remote sensing images, it is verified that the proposed method enhances the detection performance of existing state-of-the-art methods.
