AB  - To accommodate growing demand for streamlined processing of uncrewed aerial system (UAS) based hyperspectral imaging (HSI) data, an integrated raw-to-reflectance processor has been developed within the m4mining project. HSI workflows typically emphasize data calibration, geocoding, and atmospheric correction, yet data quality issues are rarely addressed using a standardized approach, and community-wide adoption of quality indicators is lagging. To address this, we present an automated Data Quality Assessment (DQA) toolbox. The DQA operates on calibrated radiance cubes and provides a standardized suite of quality metrics, including bad pixel detection, shadow masking, and band-by-band signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) estimation using a spectral differencing approach. Results are exported as a multi-layer ENVI file and summarized in a comprehensive PDF report with visualizations and recommendations. Validated with HySpex Mjolnir VS620 data from mining surveys, the toolbox enables rapid evaluation of HSI quality, supporting informed decisions before atmospheric correction and product derivation.
