AB  - To mitigate radiation instability caused by internal sensor temperature drift in uncooled multispectral infrared cameras, this paper proposes a hybrid nonuniformity correction (NUC) method utilizing an embedded reflection reference. A gold mirror embedded in the filter wheel assembly serves as a direct reference source for real-time drift tracking. The algorithm fuses the gain parameters derived from multi-point blackbody calibration with dynamic stray radiation update data from the gold mirror. Experimental results show that this method controls the average deviation within ±0.80% and limits the overall drift range to 1.16%. Compared to the traditional two-point correction method, it demonstrates a significant improvement in correcting the effects of temperature drift, and this method has high value in practical applications.
